{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, it wouldn't be to impose world peace or end disease or something like that.\n\nIt would be deeper than the outcome - I'd change the starting condition.\n\nI'd make sure every child grows up feeling fundamentally safe, loved, and like they truly belong. At least one person who is crazy about them, a full belly, a safe place to sleep, and a childhood where they don't have to be in survival mode.\n\nBecause almost everything broken in the world comes downstream of the opposite of that.\n\nWhen people don't feel safe when they're young, fear stays loud for the rest of their lives. Fear turns into hoarding, into tribalism, into needing to dominate other people, into not being able to handle hard truths. Hurt people tend to hurt people.\n\nBut a person who grew up feeling secure doesn't need to prove their worth by making someone else smaller. They have enough bandwidth left over to be curious about other people instead of threatened by them. They can handle disagreement without dehumanizing. They can think long-term.\n\nIf you changed that one thing, you wouldn't have to force peace - in a generation or two you'd have a world full of adults who *want* peace because they have the psychological safety to choose it.\n\nMy version of it is basically this: I'd make curiosity louder than fear in every human mind.\n\nWhat about you? What's your one change?",
